# Every input to a RISC Zero guest image id that is not the guest source itself,
# declared once. `scripts/install-risc0-toolchain.sh` and
# `scripts/build-zkvm-guest.sh` read this file, and every image that compiles a
# guest goes through those two scripts, so no Dockerfile repeats a value from
# here and two images cannot drift apart by editing one of them.
#
# The file is shell syntax so a `.`-source works in every image; nothing in it is
# a secret and nothing here is host-specific.
#
# What was measured on 2026-09-04, building `protocol/zkvm-reducer`'s guest eight
# times and varying one thing at a time (the table is in `IMAGE_ID.md`):
#
#   host Rust toolchain          does NOT reach the guest ELF. 1.90.0, 1.94.1 and
#                                stable 1.98.1 produce a byte-identical guest,
#                                because `risc0-build` sets RUSTC to the rzup
#                                RISC Zero rustc and compiles the guest with that.
#   CARGO_HOME                   does NOT reach it: `risc0-build` strips every
#                                CARGO* variable from the guest build.
#   the base image               does NOT reach it.
#   the four versions below      DO: they are the compiler.
#   ZKVM_GUEST_BUILD_ROOT        DOES: the guest embeds the absolute path of its
#                                own crate and of the reducer crate it shares with
#                                the host, in panic locations.
#   ZKVM_GUEST_BUILD_HOME        DOES: with CARGO_HOME stripped, the guest's cargo
#                                falls back to $HOME/.cargo, and the panic
#                                locations of every registry dependency carry it.

# `rzup install <component> <version>` with no version takes the newest of each,
# and that is how an image id moves without a source change.
RISC0_RUST_VERSION=1.88.0
RISC0_CPP_VERSION=2024.1.5
RISC0_R0VM_VERSION=3.0.3
RISC0_CARGO_RISCZERO_VERSION=3.0.3

# `risczero/risc0-guest-builder:r0.1.88.0`, the tag `risc0-build 3.0.3` defaults
# to, pinned by digest because the tag is mutable upstream. `bonsol build` runs
# the Bonsol guests inside it. Those builds get their reproducibility from this
# digest and from the fixed path the builder mounts the guest at, so the two
# values below do not apply to them.
RISC0_GUEST_BUILDER_DIGEST=sha256:3e12f71bacd27527a61dea96fa0e53e468c99aa261d3a1019b593f6dbd943eb3

# Where `scripts/build-zkvm-guest.sh` compiles the branch canonicalization guest.
# Both values are part of `protocol/zkvm-reducer/IMAGE_ID`: changing either one
# changes the id, which retires every receipt the previous guest produced. They
# are the values the pinned id was recorded from.
ZKVM_GUEST_BUILD_ROOT=/src
ZKVM_GUEST_BUILD_HOME=/root
